---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { href } from "../../lib/site";
const toc = [{ id: "commands", text: "Commands" }, { id: "init", text: "init" }, { id: "frameworks", text: "Frameworks" }, { id: "add", text: "add" }, { id: "diff", text: "diff" }, { id: "config", text: "vin.json" }, { id: "offline", text: "Offline" }];
---
<Docs title="CLI" seoTitle="VinUI CLI: Add Components and Blocks with npx · VinUI" description="npx @vinish/ui: set up a project, add components and blocks, switch styles and see upstream changes. No install, no dependencies." current="cli" toc={toc}>
  <div class="crumbs"><a href={href("/")}>VinUI</a><span>CLI</span></div>
  <h1 class="page-title">CLI</h1>
  <p class="page-lead"><code>npx</code> comes with Node.js. It downloads the small VinUI CLI, runs it and leaves nothing installed. The CLI has no dependencies.</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="commands">Commands</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Commands table">
      <table class="api">
        <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>init</code></td><td>Set up the project: framework, style, accent and folder. Writes <code>vin.json</code> and <code>vin.css</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>add &lt;names…&gt;</code></td><td>Copy components (and the ones they need) into your project. Blocks too: <code>add login-01</code> writes it to <code>blocks/</code> and adds the components it uses.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>style &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Switch the style. Rewrites <code>vin.css</code> only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>diff [names…]</code></td><td>Show what changed in VinUI since you added a component.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>list</code></td><td>List the components and blocks.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 id="init">init</h2>
    <p>Asks only what it can't work out. Every answer can be given as a flag instead, which is handy in scripts (<code>-y</code> skips the questions).</p>
    <CodeBlock title="Terminal" lang="bash" code={`npx @vinish/ui init --framework react --style tactile --accent "#0d9488" --radius lg -y`} />
    <p>The <a href={href("/create/")}>Create</a> page builds this command for you as you pick a style, accent and the rest.</p>
    <p><code>vin.css</code> starts with an <code>@import</code> of the style's fonts from Google Fonts, so they load wherever you import <code>vin.css</code>. <code>--no-fonts</code> leaves it out when you host the fonts yourself; <code>style &lt;name&gt; --fonts</code> puts it back. <code>style</code> switches the fonts together with the style.</p>

    <h2 id="frameworks">Frameworks and folders</h2>
    <p><code>init</code> reads <code>package.json</code> to pick the framework: Svelte or SvelteKit, then Vue or Nuxt, then React or Next.js. With none of them it sets up plain HTML. <code>--framework</code> overrides it.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Frameworks and folders table">
      <table class="api">
        <thead><tr><th>Framework</th><th>Files</th><th>Default folder</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>react</code></td><td><code>.tsx</code></td><td><code>src/components/vin</code> (or <code>components/vin</code> without <code>src</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>vue</code></td><td><code>.vue</code></td><td><code>src/components/vin</code> (or <code>components/vin</code> without <code>src</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>svelte</code></td><td><code>.svelte</code>, one file per part</td><td><code>src/lib/components/vin</code> in SvelteKit, else <code>src/components/vin</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>html</code></td><td>The examples as <code>.html</code>, plus <code>vinui.js</code> when needed</td><td><code>vin</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Choose another folder with <code>--path</code>. Components and blocks import each other with relative paths, so any folder works and you don't need an <code>@</code> path alias. See <a href={href("/docs/frameworks/")}>Frameworks</a> for how the versions differ.</p>

    <h2 id="add">add</h2>
    <CodeBlock title="Terminal" lang="bash" code="npx @vinish/ui add dialog dropdown-menu" />
    <p>Each component brings the ones it uses: <code>add alert-dialog</code> also adds <code>dialog</code>, and in Svelte <code>add card</code> adds <code>card-header.svelte</code> and the other parts.</p>
    <p>If you've changed a file, <code>add</code> asks before replacing it (or keeps yours with <code>-y</code>). <code>--overwrite</code> replaces without asking. Mistyped names get a suggestion.</p>

    <h2 id="diff">diff</h2>
    <CodeBlock title="Terminal" lang="bash" code="npx @vinish/ui diff button" />
    <p>Lines with <code>-</code> are yours, <code>+</code> are VinUI's. It exits with code 1 when something differs, so you can use it in CI.</p>

    <h2 id="config">vin.json</h2>
    <CodeBlock title="vin.json" lang="json" code={`{\n  "$schema": "https://vinish.dev/ui/r/vin.schema.json",\n  "framework": "react",\n  "style": "tactile",\n  "accent": "#0d9488",\n  "path": "src/components/vin",\n  "css": "src/vin.css",\n  "components": { "button": "0.1.0" }\n}`} />
    <p><code>"fonts": false</code> appears after <code>--no-fonts</code>: <code>vin.css</code> then doesn't load the fonts, and <code>style</code> keeps it that way.</p>

    <h2 id="offline">Offline and self-hosting</h2>
    <p>Components come from <code>https://vinish.dev/ui/r/</code>. Point the CLI at a folder or another server with <code>--registry</code> or the <code>VINUI_REGISTRY</code> environment variable, for example a build of this site.</p>
  </div>
</Docs>
